    "summary": "High‑energy Fox show with stellar Caution finale and Pigpen highlights",
    "blurb": "The March 18 1971 performance packs a powerful Other One suite that erupts into the rare 1971 Caution, plus a soaring Uncle John's Band. Pigpen shines on The Rub and organ‑driven moments, while the band maintains a tight, high‑energy flow throughout both sets.",
    "review": "What unfolds at the Fox Theatre on March 18 1971 is a snapshot of the Dead in top form during their early‑70s surge. The first set rolls through familiar terrain—Big Boss Man and Bertha sit comfortably beside a crunchy China Cat > I Know You Rider, while Pigpen’s organ roars on The Rub and his harmonica adds grit to Playing In The Band. The second set truly ignites: a marathon Truckin' segues into an expansive Other One suite that builds tension before launching into the iconic Caution/Feedback climax, capped by a heartfelt Uncle John's Band where Phil Lesh steps up vocally. Across all three soundboard sources the mix is surprisingly clear for the era, letting Pigpen’s keyboards and Jerry’s guitar cut through even when occasional tape drops appear. In short, this show delivers a balanced blend of tight ensemble work, inspired solos, and that rare 1971 Caution moment that makes it a must‑listen for any Deadhead.",
